# --- Retired camera slugs (added 2026-07-30) ---
# Google Search Console still ranks these five camera URLs from an earlier version
# of the camera roster; they are not in src/data/cameras.ts anymore and were
# returning hard 404s. Over the trailing 3 months they took 5 of the site's 7 total
# organic clicks and 64 of 286 impressions — i.e. most real search traffic was
# landing on a dead end. Both slash forms are listed because GSC has each indexed
# separately. 301 (not 302) because the old pages are permanently gone.
#
# Where a genuinely comparable page exists, point at it; where it doesn't, point at
# the camera directory rather than invent a match:
#   ala-moana-beach / i-h1-east -> Honolulu-area intent, /regions/hawaii has 8 cams
#   south-beach-miami -> no Florida camera in the roster at all, so /browse (the
#     full directory) is the honest target. Google may still soft-404 it; the win
#     there is user experience, not rankings.
/camera/ala-moana-beach     /regions/hawaii  301
/camera/ala-moana-beach/    /regions/hawaii  301
/camera/i-h1-east           /regions/hawaii  301
/camera/i-h1-east/          /regions/hawaii  301
/camera/south-beach-miami   /browse          301
/camera/south-beach-miami/  /browse          301

